// Golden retrieval set for the waste-law corpus. One JSON object per line; // comments allowed.
// Schema and scoring: evals/retrieval_scoring.py. Validated offline by tests/test_retrieval_golden.py.
//
// expect   — every acceptable source. `source` is a case-insensitive substring of the
//            `source_file` payload (stable across re-chunks); `law` is for humans only.
//            `articles` (optional) makes the case article-level; a case is scored at
//            article level only when every entry names its articles.
//            "none" marks an off-topic case (reported, not gated — no relevance cutoff yet).
// category — general_law | special_streams | packaging | weee | rulebook | off_topic
// split    — dev (tune against these) | holdout (never look at while tuning; run only
//            to confirm a change)
//
// Policy: keep this set fixed and append. Edit or delete a case only when it is wrong or
// the law changed, as its own reviewable commit. Every real bad answer becomes a case.
//
// Authoring: questions are written the way a business owner asks, not by copying article
// titles — a question that repeats the title only tests string overlap. Expectations were
// read from the article text in the live collection. Questions whose answer sits in
// several laws at once (inspector powers, generic penalties) are excluded unless every
// correct source is listed.

